          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I find my groundwater temperature?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Measure it. On a winter morning before anyone has used water, run a cold tap for a few minutes and hold a kitchen thermometer in the stream. If you are sizing in summer, subtract 10 to 15 degrees. Otherwise use a regional range: roughly 35 to 45 degrees in the northern states and 62 to 77 across the Gulf and Florida."
